[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines and marked known: one bug, one fix queued.
Read by what each report describes and which tenant sent it, the ticket holds three problems with
three different fixes. The queued parser fix closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Shipping the parser fix and closing #4471 leaves two bugs live: the booking-v3 date hint and a
one-day timezone shift. Each now has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/alecramos-sudo/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/alecramos-sudo/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2',
    shift: 'https://github.com/alecramos-sudo/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3',
  }}
/>

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. "Booked for 2 July. The invite says 7 February." Fix: parse in the tenant's locale.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first,
  as told, and the form reads the date day first. The parser fix does not touch it. Fix: print the
  hint from the tenant's locale.
- **`shift`**: the date moves by one day, not by a swap. "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
  Toronto got Monday. Same meeting." That is timezone handling, not parsing. Fix: keep booking dates
  as calendar dates, not midnight instants.

## How a report is placed

1. One id, one report. The export repeats some ids across overlapping pages; each counts once.
2. `shift`: the reports the desk itself read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). No day/month
   swap fits any of them.
3. `hint` and `parser`: by tenant, as `causes.ts` already does. A day-first tenant's report through
   the booking-v3 form is `hint`; any other report from a day-first tenant is `parser`.

Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. The column above shows how often it disagrees
with the tenant; the tenant decides.

## Why the ticket hid them

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. Subjects like
  "Date is wrong" fit all three bugs, so all three landed in one ticket.
- The #4471 cause table already showed `hint` as a second cause and footnoted the one-day moves
  inside `parser`. The page above it said "one issue", so neither got a ticket.
- Decision 0001 was last reviewed in June 2024. It needs a replacing record: merge on cause, not
  subject. Its deciders should write it; this page does not edit it.

